Health Potion	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Health Potion","wikiPath":"/Health_Potion","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Kerra Island","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Errrak Thickshank","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Tiger Skin","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Tiger_Skin"},{"name":"Odd Kobold Paw","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Odd_Kobold_Paw"},{"name":"Snake Fang","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Snake_Fang"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Bone Talisman","item":"Bone Talisman","wikiPath":"/Bone_Talisman"},{"text":"You gain experience!! (0.010%) @level 10"}],"card":{"title":"Health Potion","lines":["Minimum Level: 1+ (Rec. 12)","Classes: All","Related Zones: Kerra Island, Toxxulia Forest","Related NPCs: a kobold shaman, various snakes, a wild tiger"]},"links":["Kerra Island","Errrak Thickshank","Toxxulia Forest","A kobold shaman","A wild tiger","Bone Talisman","Tiger Skin","Odd Kobold Paw","Snake Fang"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Errrak Thickshank","text":"What? What do you want? My tseq, Graalf, lies sick and you waste time with talk when you [cannot help]."},{"npc":"Errrak Thickshank","text":"Mitty and her loyalists. They do not care. They do not help. The shamans, they have said I need [talismans] to ward the sickness from Graalf."},{"npc":"Errrak Thickshank","text":"Errr? You wish to help? We will see. I need a tiger's skin, from the trrraining pit south of ourrr village, for its brave spirit, an odd kobold paw carried by the forrrest kobold shamans, and a snake fang for the poison that can be made into an antidote. If you truly intend to help, then good speed and hurry!"},{"npc":"Errrak Thickshank","text":"I cannot believe. Thank you. Please, take this talisman. I bought from wandering shaman but it no help Graalf, maybe it help you. Now please go, Errrak must see if this will help Graalf."},{"npc":"Errrak Thickshank","text":"I cannot believe. Thank you. Please, take this talisman. I bought from wandering shaman but it no help Graalf, maybe it help you. Now please go, Errrak must see if this will help Graalf."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:16:56.428Z","outOfEra":false}
Fisherman Convert	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Fisherman Convert","wikiPath":"/Fisherman_Convert","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Erudin","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Dleria Mausrel","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Minor Items, Experience, Coin"}],"card":{"title":"Fisherman Convert","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: Paladin (Erudite)","Related Zones: Qeynos Aqueducts, South Qeynos","Related NPCs: Marlin Bizmite, Weligon Steelherder, Gans Paust, Bait Masterson"]},"links":["Erudin","Dleria Mausrel","Paladin","Qeynos Aqueducts","Qeynos","Marlin Bizmite","Weligon Steelherder","Gans Paust","Bait Masterson","Old Blue Tunic*","A tattered note","Deepwater Knights","High Council of Erudin","Heretics","Snapped Pole"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Dleria Mausrel","text":"Hail! You appear to be a [new priest]. Ah, I so enjoy the presence of youth within Deepwater Temple. I am sure Prexus is smiling upon us as we speak."},{"npc":"Dleria Mausrel","text":"As I suspected. I shall assist you with your training and you shall assist the temple with your service. A young priest can help out by asking to [convert fishermen in Qeynos] or maybe even something truly great such as requesting to [protect the depths]."},{"npc":"Dleria Mausrel","text":"So you wish to journey to Qeynos? So be it. Go to Qeynos and find me a willing convert. Ask them if they wish the blessing of Prexus. If so, they should snap their pole in two and you will return it to me. Do this and be rewarded."},{"npc":"Marlin Bizmite","text":"Greetings, fellow fisherman. You must be a fisherman. You have the stench of one. If you are not, might I suggest this new pastime I have heard of? A bath!!"},{"npc":"Marlin Bizmite","text":"Oh no!! Not another Prexus freak!! Listen up aqua man, if you think a man named Marlin has any chance of giving up fishing, you have got another think coming. Go night diving in the north pond, you might find some bait for your Prexus blessing."},{"npc":"Bait Masterson","text":"You know.. I took up fishing because it was a nice, quiet activity. Most of all, I took it up to avoid conversing with strangers. Get the picture?!!"},{"npc":"Bait Masterson","text":"Prexus!!? Aye!! I once followed the ways of the Ocean Lord. I remember those days. So clear and peaceful were they. I shall make a deal with you, my friend. I shall give up fishing if you give me your guild tunic. With such a tunic I shall once again be compelled to follow the peaceful ways of the Ocean Lord."},{"npc":"Dleria Mausrel","text":"Good work, young priest. Soon you shall carry the word of the Ocean Lord to distant lands. For now, continue your training. As for your reward, I have this which has been sitting in our vault. I hope it can be of use to a young priest such as yourself."},{"npc":"Bait Masterson","text":"Nice material!! I feel the ways of Prexus enlightening my soul. Unngh!! Enough of this fishing. Here take my broken fishing pole an toss it to the sea. All hail Prexus!!"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:16:57.519Z","outOfEra":false}
Become PvP (Erudin)	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Become PvP (Erudin)","wikiPath":"/Become_PvP_(Erudin)","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Erudin","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Priest of Discord","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[],"rewards":[{"text":"Tome of Order and Discord","item":"Tome of Order and Discord","wikiPath":"/Tome_of_Order_and_Discord"}],"card":{"title":"Become PvP (Erudin)","lines":["Minimum Level: 1","Classes: All","Related Zones: Erudin","Related NPCs: Priest of Discord"]},"links":["Erudin","Priest of Discord","Tome of Order and Discord"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Priest of Discord","text":"Greetings, ______. Are you a child of Order? If you have come seeking the path of Discord, I require only that you give me your [Tome of Order and Discord] and I shall show you the way. Only then will you be freed from Order's confining restraints."},{"npc":"Priest of Discord","text":"The Tome of Order and Discord was penned by the seventh member of the Tribunal and has become the key to a life of Discord, in spite of the author's pitiful warnings. Do you not have one, child of Order? Would you [like to read] it?"},{"npc":"Priest of Discord","text":"Very well. Here you go. Simply return it to me to be released from the chains of Order."},{"npc":"Priest of Discord","text":"I see you wish to join us in Discord! Welcome! By turning your back on the protection of Order you are now open to many more opportunities for glory and power. Remember that you can now be harmed by those who have also heard the call of Discord."}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T09:57:54.028Z","outOfEra":false}
